[ar:Slim Dusty]
[al:The Very Best Of Slim Dusty]
[ti:We've Done Us Proud]
[00:01.47] We've done us proud to come this far,
[00:09.16] Down through the years to where we are,
[00:17.36] Side by side, hand in hand, we've lived and died,
[00:28.91] For this great land, we've done us proud.
[00:37.34] I sailed the seas in search of freedom,
[00:45.22] I tilled the soil for seed to grow,
[00:52.77] I built the fences to hold the cattle,
[01:00.71] I mined the earth in search of gold.
[01:08.86] I sheared the sheep of golden fleeces,
[01:16.78] I formed the union, to win fair pay,
[01:24.93] I built a railroad to cross the country,
[01:32.99] I fought a war for the countrys sake.
[01:40.65] We've done us proud to come this far
[01:48.76] Down through the years to where we are
[01:56.91] Side by side, hand in hand, we've lived and died,
[02:08.68] For this great land, we've done us proud
[02:16.77] I kept a home and raised a family,
[02:24.59] I taught your children as if my own,
[02:32.01] I painted pictures to show the beauty,
[02:40.00] I wrote the stories to keep the flame.
[02:48.22] We've done us proud to come this far
[02:56.19] Down through the years to where we are
[03:04.46] Side by side, hand in hand, we've lived and died,
